# What NOT to send into the Docker build context.
#
# The web image is built from the REPO ROOT (the workspace root package.json and
# package-lock.json must be in context), so without this file Docker tars up the
# entire tree — ~13 GB here — before the build even starts.
#
# Mirrors .vercelignore, with two differences that matter:
#   - `apps/web/models` is excluded as a DIRECTORY, not just `model.bin`. It is
#     288 MB of Opus MT weights, untracked in git, and translation runs through
#     Anthropic and the Railway worker instead.
#   - package.json / package-lock.json must NOT be excluded. `npm ci` needs them
#     and the Dockerfile copies them in its own layer for caching.

node_modules
**/node_modules
.next
**/.next
out
dist

# Agent worktrees: 9 GB of full repo copies, each with its own node_modules.
.claude/worktrees

.git
.github
*.log
coverage
playwright-report
test-results

# Never bake environment files into an image. Railway injects its own env vars,
# and a .env.local landing in the build would override them at build time —
# which for NEXT_PUBLIC_* means the wrong value is inlined into the client
# bundle with nothing to signal it.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.production.example

# Local import staging. LOCAL_IMPORTS_DIR defaults here, so it fills up with
# real manuscripts as authors import them.
.uploads

# Opus MT weights — 288 MB, see header.
apps/web/models

# Python virtualenvs.
.venv
**/.venv

# Local agent/tooling state, not application code.
.gstack
.swarm
.claude-flow
.ds-sync
.design-sync
.remember
.serena

# Docs and tests do not belong in a runtime image.
docs
tests
e2e

.DS_Store
